    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1909/document/15> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493338436/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """so there can’t be much in my beloved “Radiozone”!A Mr. Eno who sat by me was very nice, also his wife, who is a great believer in the spiritual power for Good of Mrs. Piper. She had an illness, in the course of which  everything changed  for her. She couldn’t explain it very clearly.
I had a long talk with the musician son, Courtlandt Palmer — rather interesting. He is afraid of becoming a Catholic. I said I had been one, and it never hurt me, so far as I could tell.  It must be taken aesthetically.
Mrs. Fabbri was there, chattering like a parrot on the the most serious subjects. They all said that “Equal Suffrage” was becoming quite a fashionable fad."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 15 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1909> .

